  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhile implementing servo/servo#50044, I noticed that [topmost clicked popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#topmost-clicked-popover) doesn't handle targetPopover or clickedPopover being null.\n\nSteps 1 sets clickedPopover to the result [nearest inclusive open popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#nearest-inclusive-open-popover). That algorithm can return null, but in Step 3 it is then assumed that the clickedPopover is not null and the popover stack position can be calculated. The same applies to step 2 setting targetPopover to the result of [nearest inclusive target popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#nearest-inclusive-target-popover), but that algorithm does not specify a return type and is ambiguous about the case where no popover is found (see #13298).\n\nI am not quite sure what the engines to, but a possible fix might be to return the other popover when one is null:\n\n> 3. If clickedPopover is null, then return targetPopover.\n> 4. If targetPopover is null, then return clickedPopover.",
